Member variables


Variable declarations that appear within the body of a class are 
member variables
:


class A {
  c:C;
  d:D;
}



An object of the class type contains instantiations of these member variables, which may be accessed with the dot (
.
) operator:


f(a.c);
f(a.d);



Member functions


Function declarations that appear within the body of a class are 
member functions
:


class A {
  function f(b:B, c:C) -
 D {
    // ...
